title: 'Missions wait mostly on Claude: the tests take 8% of all working time, and 23% of a build mission''s.'
pid: 8eaadf31-7921-49f5-9c46-2b05b6138cd0
body: |2-
  Measured from every Claude session's log since 2026-11-10, timing each
  command or step from its start to its result.
  The suite is slow by setting more than by hardware: it runs the Rust
  tests one at a time, runs the integration tests one at a time, and
  one integration test waits about 40 s, probably for nothing. On four
  efficiency cores it used under one core on average. So a bigger
  machine would not speed it much, and a smaller one would not slow it
  much.
  At least 20 minutes in those five days were sessions waiting for
  another session's build or tests to finish, because two suites
  cannot run at once: the integration tests edit their fixtures in place.
  What would shorten missions most is fewer or shorter back-and-forths
  with Claude, which no machine buys.
  If you do not answer, the suite stays as it is.
contains:
- 7c6b072c-c7d0-425a-9881-989509755213
- 298e4215-c5b7-4b91-a6db-591e73f3e341
